        {
          "question": "q-333428",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=2x{y}^{2},\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $\u0394x=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071464/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "9d4048e88930a83d503b4b90faa9804bf5c56b2dd1b33a64a0d8011cd4b54d3f"
        }
      ],
