          "reviewer_session": "01a118ea-3923-70c2-acd9-0830602bde5f",
          "rationale": "The trapezoidal update is Y=y+(h/2)[f(x,y)+f(x+h,Y)]. With x=y=h=1 and f(x,y)=2xy\u00b2, this becomes Y=1+(1/2)[2+4Y\u00b2]=2+2Y\u00b2. Moving terms left yields g(Y)=Y-2Y\u00b2-2, exactly original option 3. The authentic worked solution derives this expression and the screenshot grades that option Correct. The stored expression has the same function argument, coefficients, power and signs; only subscript formatting differs. The question asks for the residual function, whose derivation remains valid even though this step has no real root.",
